d description</span></summary><div class="docblock"><p>Builder-style structure used to create a <a href="struct.WasiCtx.html" title="struct wasmtime_wasi::WasiCtx"><code>WasiCtx</code></a>.</p>
<p>This type is used to create a <a href="struct.WasiCtx.html" title="struct wasmtime_wasi::WasiCtx"><code>WasiCtx</code></a> that is considered per-<a href="https://docs.rs/wasmtime/45.0.1/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/wasmtime/runtime/store/struct.Store.html" title="struct wasmtime::runtime::store::Store"><code>Store</code></a>
state. The <a href="struct.WasiCtxBuilder.html#method.build" title="method wasmtime_wasi::WasiCtxBuilder::build"><code>build</code></a> method is used to finish the
building process and produce a finalized <a href="struct.WasiCtx.html" title="struct wasmtime_wasi::WasiCtx"><code>WasiCtx</code></a>.</p>
--
<li>no arguments</li>
<li>no preopens</li>
<li>clocks use the host implementation of wall/monotonic clocks</li>
<li>RNGs are all initialized with random state and suitable generator
quality to satisfy the requirements of WASI APIs.</li>
<li>TCP/UDP are allowed but all addresses are denied by default.</li>
<li><code>wasi:sockets/ip-name-lookup</code> is denied by default.</li>
--
